  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Mr. Pr and Ms. Ad are at aaa and bbb respectively on an infinite number line. Mr. Pr wants to meet Ms. Ad.\n\nMr. Pr can choose to move  ccc or ddd units in 1 second. If Mr. Pr moves ccc units then Ms. Ad will move ddd units and vice versa. (Both of them always moved in positive x-direction)\n\nYou have to determine if Mr. Pr can meet with Ms. Ad after some integral amount of time, given that Mr. Pr chooses optimally. Note that meeting after a fractional amount of time does not count.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nEach testcase contains four space separated integers, aaa, bbb, ccc, and ddd.\n###Output:\n\n\nFor each test case, output a single line containing \"YES\" if Mr. Pr meets with Ms. Ad, otherwise \"NO\".\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105\n1≤a,b,c,d≤1091 \\leq a,b,c,d \\leq 10^91≤a,b,c,d≤109",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
